From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:24:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Docs/mm/damon/design: update node_eligible_mem_bp for changed
 behavior

DAMOS quota goal type node_eligible_mem_bp quota was accounting for
regions that eligible by only the DAMOS access pattern.  The behavior is
now changed to also account for DAMOS core filters.  Update the document
to cover the new behavior.

Signed-off-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
---
 Documentation/mm/damon/design.rst | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/mm/damon/design.rst b/Documentation/mm/damon/design.rst
index 2ff8bc6fb9f9..98d2cb8854a7 100644
--- a/Documentation/mm/damon/design.rst
+++ b/Documentation/mm/damon/design.rst
@@ -853,8 +853,8 @@ auto-tuning mechanism tries to make ``current_value`` of ``complement``-ed
   (1/10,000).
 - ``inactive_mem_bp``: Inactive to active + inactive (LRU) memory size ratio in
   bp (1/10,000).
-- ``node_eligible_mem_bp``: Scheme target access pattern-eligible memory ratio
-  of a node in bp (1/10,000).
+- ``node_eligible_mem_bp``: Scheme action eligible memory ratio of a node in bp
+  (1/10,000).
 - ``hugepage_mem_bp``: Total huge page to total used memory ratio in bp
   (1/10,000).
 
-- 
2.47.3

